                <invention-title lang="fr">TURBORÉACTEUR À ENGRENAGES AVEC PROTECTION CONTRE LA SURVITESSE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">GEARED TURBOFAN WITH OVERSPEED PROTECTION</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A gas turbine engine (100) has a fan drive turbine (114) driving a gear reduction, the gear reduction (106), in turn, driving a fan rotor (102), the fan rotor (102) delivering air into a bypass duct as bypass air and into a compressor section (24) as core flow. A forward bearing (82) is positioned between the gear reduction (106) and the fan rotor (102) and supports the gear reduction (106). A second bearing (124) is positioned aft of the gear reduction (106) and supports the gear reduction (106). The second bearing (124) is a thrust bearing (124). A fan drive turbine drive shaft (126) drives the gear reduction (106). The fan drive turbine drive shaft (126) has a weakened link (128) which is aft of the second bearing (124) such that the fan drive turbine drive shaft (126) will tend to fail at the weakened link (128), and at a location aft of the second bearing (124).</p>
            </abstract>
